e. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=-1.$ In this case,  ${f}^{′}(-1)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=0$” is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case, the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=0,$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a local minimum at $x=1$” is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=1$ since $f(1)\\le f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, all three statements are true." :task-item/_content [{:db/id 17592186729512 :task-item/content {:db/id 17592186238006} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 28.62 :task-item/id #uuid "150a4d42-836a-4fb1-b42b-b6e9964659ec" :task-item/next {:db/id 17592186729513} :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "d2a8359a-378f-5d30-b9c0-f8c4d4fb9c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461280} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3f2ac5-9e21-5c73-81bb-3e709f16ae1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461282} {:answer/id #uuid "9d12003a-0d3f-510e-b2aa-cfbebcab6a56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461284} {:answer/id #uuid "e79b52d0-6b85-5411-84b7-5e56627db8e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186667790}] :task-item/status {:db/ident :task-item.status/correct} :task-item/working-ended-at "2026-10-28T16:44:41.374Z"}]} {:db/id 17592186238008 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b0d9d1-e47c-54ba-9b31-b33369664b09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186235800} {:answer/id #uuid "58c8a29d-6f8d-5816-90cd-1987524d814c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id 17592186236376} {:answer/id #uuid "87aa58ba-7fe0-58ce-9c4e-cf7b09d0af52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/id 17592186236664} {:answer/id #uuid "956d5ea6-81ef-5247-b6ca-c5c4ad5b1297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186236765} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f3abd4-2dce-5449-bff6-569d90a5f30d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186236879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00b0d9d1-e47c-54ba-9b31-b33369664b09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186235800} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2db27c7-6dec-54c4-b324-46dcaa54ec46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186237713}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "941a791b-cbcb-5dd5-898e-ada869b3a20f" :question/math-academy-id "q-103442" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7dc7480c7ee27073ff7be7475161742e317b30bf0c3e35af33dc93a772e6034a.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- $f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=-1$\n- $f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=-1.$ In this case,  ${f}^{′}(-1)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=1.$ In this case,  ${f}^{′}(-1)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement III is false. The function has a local minimum at $x=3$ since $f(3)\\le f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statements II and III are false."} {:db/id 17592186329838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186064273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b5ea4a7-acc4-5825-b6c5-b6c87e6a1674" :knowledge-point/title "Iden