re is a sharp corner, so ${f}^{′}(4)$ doesn't exist\n\n![](images/60/60f26a8aa758ae20b2b56325d822379d407276ffd6987f56a1e7934a6406c4d2.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, there are two critical points, and their $x$-coordinates are $x=2$ and $x=4.$" :task-item/_content [{:db/id 17592186729498 :task-item/content {:db/id 17592186329838} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 13.139000000000001 :task-item/id #uuid "f961504c-45e8-49f8-9d42-6eabc15cc3bd" :task-item/next {:db/id 17592186729510} :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "a0749e1a-ee3d-512b-859b-7f4078d0db89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=4$" :db/id 17592186328322}] :task-item/status {:db/ident :task-item.status/correct} :task-item/working-ended-at "2026-10-28T16:43:40.321Z"}]} {:db/id 17592186329839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186064273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b5ea4a7-acc4-5825-b6c5-b6c87e6a1674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Critical and Stationary Points of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6180aa54-e47c-5045-96dc-d6eb10236078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All points in the closed interval $[1,5]$" :db/id 17592186327785} {:answer/id #uuid "68cc7e3e-0a69-5db2-890e-431c0fda202b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1$ only" :db/id 17592186327838} {:answer/id #uuid "6e10d0e9-6028-5c2e-91cb-f1ca26face0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1$ and $x=5$ only" :db/id 17592186327888} {:answer/id #uuid "994e309b-55c5-5877-87a1-2e9f09aa18e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=5$ only" :db/id 17592186328258} {:answer/id #uuid "f3eac55a-cd29-5f9d-b57d-2607dc053e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id 17592186329066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6180aa54-e47c-5045-96dc-d6eb10236078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All points in the closed interval $[1,5]$" :db/id 17592186327785} :answer-field/id #uuid "866bfbd0-c250-59be-9290-537b862c2ed7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186329404}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbc920c3-0ad5-5d73-9fe4-65007b1cfa41" :question/math-academy-id "q-47915" :question/problem "![](images/74/748abf694eac3c4e59fd09d3bc48648fe30e46561f536f9f9a16eac7eb526558.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is shown above. What are the $x$-coordinates of all the critical points?" :question/worked-solution "The critical points of $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ where ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(x)$ doesn't exist. Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal or where the tangent does not exist, respectively.\n\nIn the given graph, we can see that\n\n- at any point between  $x=1$ and $x=5$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ and\n\n- at $x=1$ and at $x=5$  there are sharp corners, hence ${f}^{′}(1)$ and ${f}^{′}(5)$ don't exist.\n\n![](images/48/48b786a6b9c270336ce507525acf2503439b2424dba59ed9ea200830a79dd828.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, all numbers in the closed interval $[1,5]$ are critical points for $f(x).$" :task-item/_content [{:db/id 17592186729497 :task-item/content {:db/id 17592186329839} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 54.975 :task-item/id #uuid "89397765-8c8e-44eb-860d-497ecbd26244" :task-item/next {:db/id 17592186729498} :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "6180aa54-e47c-5045-96dc-d6eb10236078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All points in the closed interval $[1,5]$" :db/id 17592186327785}] :task-item/status {:db/ident :task-item.status/correct} :task-item/working-ended-at "2026-10-28T16:43:23.336Z"}]} {:db/id 17592186329920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fc7d5d6-a451-5962-afc9-9fff555f20ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186467620} {:answer/id #uuid "80618245-4ae0-5579-a15a-1159b6d87793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186467621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80618245-4ae0-5579-a15a-1159b6d87793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186467621} :answer-field/id #uuid "2697fbf1-11b6-59e7-a243-ede0e967f0fe" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186468531} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0f9f4c1-1b21-59f3-8a3f-07dc9f40bdf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186467622} {:answer/id #uuid "250ef74c-ffc2-556d-a0a3-798c3e88030d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186467623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0f9f4c1-1b21-59f3-8a3f-07dc9f40bdf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186467622} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8df5920-44fd-5cbe-9f0a-2111cda02c34" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186468532} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5889732e-c51e-5840-9f31-81e7f3e6b2f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186467624} {:answer/id #uuid "762ae4d9-bf4c-5ca6-bb90-84a859083154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186467625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5889732e-c51e-5840-9f31-81e7f3e6b2f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186467624} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2facf3b-7a9b-53cc-9a3f-b2a9bf7a9c24" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186468533}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "101d0c36-a705-552a-b14b-442022f64eda" :question/math-academy-id "q-48734" :question/problem "![](images/14/14fdc374842064ad40ebbadf3dab16191ecfdeec8c416b4e7f17beffce44fb40.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=3$” is true. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=3.$ In this case,  ${f}^{′}(3)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=3$” is false. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the derivative is undefined at $x=3$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=3$” is false. The function does not have a local maximum at $x=3$ since $f(3)\\le f(x)$ for $x$ close enough  to the point $x=3,$ so,  actually,  $f(x)$ has local minimum at $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, only statement “$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=3$” is true." :task-item/_content [{:db/id 17592186729513 :task-item/content {:db/id 17592186329920} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 88.80199999999999 :task-item/id #uuid "55cda11c-e7b4-478d-911f-a2cd7dcdfb84" :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "80618245-4ae0-5579-a15a-1159b6d87793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186467621} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f9f4c1-1b21-59f3-8a3f-07dc9f40bdf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186467622} {:answer/id #uuid "5889732e-c51e-5840-9f31-81e7f3e6b2f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186467624}] :task-item/status {:db/ident :task-item.status/correct} :task-item/working-ended-at "2026-10-28T16:46:15.789Z"}]} {:db/id 17592186329921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e1f3def-98d2-524a-b778-f7e66a7f3296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186467626} {:answer/id #uuid "0b1a3726-de03-5ff7-9514-9c9aa55b2a6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186467627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b1a3726-de03-5ff7-9514-9c9aa55b2a6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186467627} :answer-field/id #uuid "86fbad27-f24f-5ab5-9dc2-2649e548b79d" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has  a stationary point at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186468534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "956e3925-042a-5383-b9cd-d81e8467a088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186467628} {:answer/id #uuid "906240b1-a7be-5057-81ba-1361d1041439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186467629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "906240b1-a7be-5057-81ba-1361d1041439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186467629} :answer-field/id #uuid "98dade12-9621-5587-bfac-2f8ef6ab2b14" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has  a local maximum at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186468535} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b46b1cc-def4-5734-bd89-8f1d5131c333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186467630} {:answer/id #uuid "d1649fad-0b66-52f0-b7d5-6860409aa309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186467631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1649fad-0b66-52f0-b7d5-6860409aa309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186467631} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4e72066-eadb-5611-801e-ce8cccffd34f" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186468536}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a5dfd5ad-23a9-54fc-83bf-a64cab147aed" :question/math-academy-id "q-48737" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4a2298a8255a86c803560793658593a22f7f77590ef350c1e0cebd974fce7750.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has  a stationary point at $x=0$” is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=0$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has  a local maximum at $x=2$” is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=2$ since $f(2)\\ge f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=2.$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=2$” is true. The graph of the function has a sharp edge (corner) at $x=2$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(2)$ does not exist. Hence, $x=2$ is a critical point of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, all statements are true."} {:db/id 17592186341964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186064273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b5ea4a7-acc4-5825-b6c5-b6c87e6a1674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Critical and Stationary Points of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a3673b0-4a4b-5978-9998-fd955397085d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-1$  and $x=7$" :db/id 17592186339649} {:answer/id #uuid "53b9d09f-9007-5ada-976c-2e012373060d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-1$ only" :db/id 17592186339903} {:answer/id #uuid "9b89a2ad-7549-5777-b588-f5c02bee4ae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=3$ and $x=7$" :db/id 17592186340528} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf1e416-8b63-5226-ad41-f7ddb3b203bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=3$ only" :db/id 17592186340531} {:answer/id #uuid "a08ef0df-6431-539d-898e-096e5fd97852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=7$ only" :db/id 17592186340583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b89a2ad-7549-5777-b588-f5c02bee4ae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=3$ and $x=7$" :db/id 17592186340528} :answer-field/id #uuid "73132585-cc94-5a40-bbc3-351536964fa5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186341581}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f2ec4d2-9f1a-59c8-aeba-911dc271f39d" :question/math-academy-id "q-73399" :question/problem "![](images/43/432991e403167bd560517072d24058c3f2106f093cdcad08f3b5f0ed486f9504.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the critical points?" :question/worked-solution "The critical points of $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ where ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(x)$ doesn't exist. Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal or where the tangent does not exist, respectively. \n\nIn the given graph, we can see that \n\n- at $x=3$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${f}^{′}(3)=0,$ while\n\n- at $x=7$ there is a discontinuity, so  ${f}^{′}(7)$ doesn't exist.\n\n![](images/e0/e035d64e759108be78c54d0d8d1018906ef253bdcdaff548edd185b8b6543505.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, there are two critical points, and their $x$-coordinates are $x=3$ and $x=7.$" :task-item/_content [{:db/id 17592186729440 :task-item/content {:db/id 17592186341964} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 37.998999999999995 :task-item/id #uuid "c9e913df-6481-4284-bf15-6fc79eee5170" :task-item/next {:db/id 17592186729497} :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "9bf1e416-8b63-5226-ad41-f7ddb3b203bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=3$ only" :db/id 17592186340531}] :task-item/status {:db/ident :task-item.status/incorrect} :task-item/working-ended-at "2026-10-28T16:41:41.172Z"}]} {:db/id 17592186341965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186064273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b5ea4a7-acc4-5825-b6c5-b6c87e6a1674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Critical and Stationary Points of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aee028a-5473-56b8-aee5-bdb011708151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=0$ and $x=2$" :db/id 17592186339222} {:answer/id #uuid "38edbb45-8a8f-5c9f-89e6-a14df9e79c49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=6$ only" :db/id 17592186339640} {:answer/id #uuid "4c17b524-97bf-5d55-bc46-acf8d26004be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=2$ only" :db/id 17592186339813} {:answer/id #uuid "62113950-85db-5a6d-98d6-ae248b3847ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/id 17592186340002} {:answer/id #uuid "d6ac01be-6526-5f9f-b3ca-56e460493d3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=6$" :db/id 17592186341031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62113950-85db-5a6d-98d6-ae248b3847ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/id 17592186340002} :answer-field/id #uuid "a711b931-a46e-513a-9ac0-e43329d1aa18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186341671}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3747ead0-6028-5b33-a0a9-4b842fbf83b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-73401" :question/problem "![](images/48/48569328379c72215884b759687c7c40ced06f9864d05d2638e4389694f90630.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the stationary points?" :question/worked-solution "A stationary point of $f(x)$ is the value of $x$ where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal.\n\nIn the given graph, we can see that at $x=0,$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${f}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\n![](images/57/576d25a420f1f4ebcbd0e9b055d7a27159caa8f1721ff5f35a32b86c3e3a0fb3.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, there is only one stationary point, and its $x$-coordinate is $x=0.$\n\n**Note:** At $x=2$, there is a sharp corner, so ${f}^{′}(2)$ doesn't exist. This gives one more critical point. But this is not a stationary point." :task-item/_content [{:db/id 17592186729422 :task-item/content {:db/id 17592186341965} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 21.574 :task-item/id #uuid "069e03e8-6fd5-4015-81a8-2af125dcd7df" :task-item/next {:db/id 17592186729440} :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "62113950-85db-5a6d-98d6-ae248b3847ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/id 17592186340002}] :task-item/status {:db/ident :task-item.status/correct} :task-item/working-ended-at "2026-10-28T16:40:26.086Z"}]} {:db/id 17592186402902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4d23575-4aa4-50b3-8f45-fa5b80561dfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186473154} {:answer/id #uuid "ed8e14b7-e1aa-5f72-99fe-d0d63eed18da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186473155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4d23575-4aa4-50b3-8f45-fa5b80561dfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186473154} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f3e8587-e9da-5d96-9590-a8b34259c744" :answer-field/key "Point $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/chec